      children: "Enterprise software systems are distinguished from smaller projects not just by size but by a cluster of interrelated properties that fundamentally change the nature of engineering work. These systems typically serve large, heterogeneous user bases with divergent needs, operate under strict availability and performance requirements, and must integrate with a landscape of legacy systems, third-party services, and internal platforms that evolve on their own schedules."
