      children: "Software architecture is the set of significant design decisions that shape a system's structure, behavior, and quality attributes. Significant decisions are those that are costly to reverse, affect large portions of the system, or directly determine whether key quality requirements can be met. Architectural decisions include choices of deployment topology, data storage strategies, service decomposition boundaries, communication protocols, and cross-cutting mechanisms such as authentication, logging, and error handling."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
