      children: "The two primary paradigms in contemporary software engineering are plan-driven development and agile development. Plan-driven development, associated with waterfall and V-model approaches, emphasizes upfront planning, comprehensive documentation, and sequential phase completion. It is well-suited to contexts where requirements are stable and well-understood, where regulatory compliance requires detailed documentation, or where the cost of errors (as in safety-critical systems) justifies extensive validation before execution."
    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
